      "title": "Katy Perry slams White House after using her song 'Firework' in military strike video",
      "description": "Katy Perry is speaking out after the White House's official TikTok account used her song \u201cFirework\u201d in a video showing footage of military strikes. The video, posted last Thursday, featured lyrics from her Grammy-nominated album \"Teenage Dream\", including the words \"boom, boom, boom,\" played over clips of bombs exploding. Its caption read: \"Iran has been warned.\" Expressing her frustration, Katy posted on X (formerly known as Twitter), saying, \"I am deeply appalled and angry to see \u2018Firework\u2019 used on the @WhiteHouse TikTok account as a backing track for video footage of military strikes. I did not approve this, I was not asked, and I absolutely do not condone it.\" \u201cI wrote this song to be an anthem of hope, healing, and inner strength for people going through their darkest personal moments,\u201d she continued. \"To see a message of self-worth and upliftment weaponized to soundtrack destruction and violence is a complete violation of everything my song stands for.\" Katy concluded her statement: \"My music is for bringing people together, not celebrating warfare.\" Earlier this year, Kesha condemned the White House for using her song \"Blow\" on TikTok featuring fighter jets in the sky with the caption, \"Lethality.\"",
      "link": "https://mb.com.ph/article/10928425/entertainment/music-and-concerts/katy-perry-slams-white-house-after-using-her-song-firework-in-military-strike-video",
